(CRISPR-Cas9 Endonuclease Mechanisms and Genome Editing Precision) Tj T*
(Laboratory of Molecular Genetics and Gene Therapy) Tj T*
(1. Bacterial Adaptive Immunity and Guide RNA Hybridization) Tj T*
(The Type II CRISPR-Cas9 system from Streptococcus pyogenes uses a dual RNA guide consisting of) Tj T*
(CRISPR RNA \(crRNA\) and trans-activating crRNA \(tracrRNA\), engineered into a single guide RNA \(sgRNA\).) Tj T*
(2. Protospacer Adjacent Motif \(PAM\) Recognition and Double-Strand Breaks) Tj T*
(Target DNA cleavage requires a canonical 5'-NGG-3' PAM sequence immediately adjacent to the 20-nucleotide protospacer.) Tj T*
(Cas9 catalyzes double-stranded breaks via two endonuclease domains:) Tj T*
(- RuvC domain: cleaves the non-target DNA strand) Tj T*
(- HNH domain: cleaves the target DNA strand complementary to the gRNA) Tj T*
(3. DNA Repair Pathways: NHEJ vs HDR) Tj T*
(Table 1: Comparison of Cas9 repair outcomes.) Tj T*
(Pathway | Template Required | Error Rate | Primary Outcome) Tj T*
(NHEJ    | None              | High \(InDels\) | Gene Knockout / Frameshift) Tj T*
(HDR     | Exogenous Donor   | High Fidelity | Precision Gene Knock-in / Point Mutation) Tj T*
(Figure 1 \(Page 1\): Crystal structure depiction of Cas9-sgRNA ribonucleoprotein complex bound to DNA target.) Tj T*
